	(footprint "TT:K3599_TRS_6leg"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "2e5efdd5-eab0-4474-b10d-ff902c4017bc")
		(at 140.775 77.86 180)
		(descr "Mantech K3599 1/4in (6.35mm) 3-conductor CLOSED (switched) open-frame phone jack, 6 solder lugs. MEASURED off the real part 2026-10-10 (recalibrated caliper): thin leg 1.34mm (through the board), along-row pitch 6.36mm c-c (3 legs/row), row spacing 16.55mm c-c (17.89 outside-to-outside - 1.34 leg; legs FLEX in this direction so holes are generous), lug width 20mm, jack length 34.12mm, barrel axis 12.39mm below the board (bottom-mount drop). Barrel/bushing IN LINE with the legs at the +Y (back-wall) end; body extends -Y (forward, below the board). Pads 1/2/3 = Tip/Ring/Sleeve, CONFIRMED off the part 2026-10-10: TIP is furthest from the barrel opening (deepest, pad 1 at -Y); RING is the middle leg (pad 2); SLEEVE/GND is closest to the opening (pad 3 at +Y, the barrel end) -- matches the Conn_01x03 symbol pins 1/2/3. Barrel front = panel hole = +18.36 from the ring leg (12 from the sleeve leg, 7 from back-of-barrel to the tip leg). The 3 unnumbered pads are the switch/normalling lugs (soldered, no net in v1). BOTTOM-MOUNTED: place on B.Cu so the body hangs below the board.")
		(tags "jack TRS 6.35mm phone K3599 open-frame switched measured")
